%% Full detailed pipeline — companion diagram to architecture-document.md.
%% This is the "big" architecture diagram (for the 2-page doc / your own
%% understanding), NOT the simplified one used on the PPT slide — that one is
%% documents/idea-ppt/technical-approach-diagram.mmd and deliberately drops
%% most of this detail for a 3-second read. Read architecture-document.md
%% section 3 alongside this; the numbers below match that section's steps.

flowchart TD

    F0[/"Config file(s) — single or bulk upload<br/>CLI text OR structured JSON/YAML"/]

    F0 --> S1["1. Input-sanity gate<br/>reject non-config junk before it burns quota"]

    S1 --> S2["2. Redaction pass<br/>regex secret-shapes + entropy fallback<br/>raw original stored encrypted-at-rest"]

    S2 --> S3A["3a. Fingerprint vendor + version<br/>signature match, then embedding fallback"]
    S2 --> S3B["3b. Device-ID extraction<br/>(parallel, always runs)"]

    S3A --> S3C["3c. Structured-config normalizer<br/>(JSON/YAML sources only)<br/>flattens but preserves cross-references"]

    S3C --> S35["3.5 Cross-reference / linking stage<br/>joins controls split by NAME not proximity<br/>(AAA method-lists, policy names, SG-to-SG refs)"]

    S35 --> KB{{"4. resolve_unit(unit, vendor_context)<br/>ONE function, ONE knowledge base"}}

    KB -- "Tier 1: similarity &ge; 0.85<br/>cache hit, auto-mapped" --> NORM
    KB -- "Tier 2: 0.4&ndash;0.85<br/>LLM proposes mapping + reasoning" --> LLM
    KB -- "Tier 3: &lt; 0.4 or human-rejected<br/>review queue" --> LLM

    LLM["LLM candidate: field, value,<br/>confidence, reasoning<br/>(model/prompt version recorded)<br/>schema-validated — malformed/<br/>hallucinated output or provider<br/>outage routes to Tier 3, never crashes"] --> HITL

    HITL(("Human confirms, corrects,<br/>or rejects (reviewer role)")) --> KBW

    KBW[("Knowledge Base<br/>append-only, versioned, tenant-scoped<br/>+ periodic spot-recheck of Tier-1 entries")]

    KBW -. "same store — Tier 1 and Tier 2/3<br/>both read AND write here" .-> KB

    NORM["5. Normalize &rarr; Canonical Security Baseline Model<br/>NIST 800-53 control-family backbone<br/>scalar + list-valued fields<br/>parse_coverage_pct BY SEVERITY<br/>full field-level provenance"]
    S3B --> NORM

    NORM --> FSEL["User selects framework(s)<br/>CIS / STIG / NIST 800-53 / ISO"]

    FSEL --> RULE["6. Rule engine (deterministic, no LLM)<br/>6 predicate types incl. ORDERED/first-match<br/>for ACL &amp; security-group precedence<br/>versioned rule files per framework"]

    RULE --> VERDICT{"Finding.result"}
    VERDICT -->|"required field resolved"| PF["PASS / FAIL"]
    VERDICT -->|"required field never resolved"| NE["NOT_EVALUATED<br/>(fail-closed — never a silent PASS)"]

    PF --> SNAP["Evaluation snapshot pinned:<br/>rule_version, kb_entry_version, timestamp<br/>+ framework-version drift flag if standard revised"]
    NE --> SNAP

    SNAP --> REM["7. Remediation<br/>KB template &rarr; LLM draft (grammar-validated)<br/>&rarr; ALWAYS human-gated before shipping"]

    REM --> RPT["8. Per-device PDF report<br/>pass/fail/not_evaluated + severity + remediation<br/>+ evidence (source unit + KB provenance)<br/>+ confidence tier / review-status per finding<br/>+ device ID + parse coverage by severity"]

    RPT --> ROLLUP["Batch summary rolls up every device in the upload"]

    ROLLUP --> OUT[/"PDF report(s)"/]

    OBS1[["Langfuse<br/>traces every LLM call + human score<br/>golden-set dataset evals, versioned by prompt/model"]]
    OBS2[["Plain stats page for this build &#40;Prometheus + Grafana is the<br/>stated production target&#41;<br/>tier distribution &middot; parse coverage by severity<br/>review-queue age &middot; NOT_EVALUATED trend &middot; spot-recheck rate"]]
    LLM -.-> OBS1
    HITL -.-> OBS1
    KB -.-> OBS2
    RULE -.-> OBS2
    REM -.-> OBS2

    classDef gate fill:#595959,stroke:#333,color:#fff
    classDef redact fill:#4BACC6,stroke:#2f8a9e,color:#fff
    classDef resolve fill:#8064A2,stroke:#5f4a7d,color:#fff
    classDef norm fill:#4F81BD,stroke:#2f5c8a,color:#fff
    classDef rule fill:#1F497D,stroke:#12305a,color:#fff
    classDef remediate fill:#F79646,stroke:#c9761c,color:#fff
    classDef report fill:#9BBB59,stroke:#77953f,color:#fff
    classDef fail fill:#C0504D,stroke:#8f3a36,color:#fff

    class S1 gate
    class S2,S3A,S3B,S3C,S35 redact
    class LLM,HITL resolve
    class NORM,FSEL norm
    class RULE,VERDICT rule
    class REM remediate
    class RPT,ROLLUP,OUT report
    class NE fail
    class OBS1,OBS2 obs

    classDef obs fill:#F2F2F2,stroke:#999,color:#333,stroke-dasharray: 4 3
